User: 24 gallons per second of water flows down a waterfall. If you have an empty basin that can hold 260 gallons of water. The basin leaks water at 4 gallons per second. how long would it take to fill the basin with water from the waterfall in seconds? Write your answer in \boxed{} format.

Assistant: To find the time it takes to fill the basin with water from the waterfall, we need to find the rate at which water from the waterfall enters the basin. The rate at which water enters the basin is the rate of water from the waterfall minus the rate of leakage, which is 24 - 4 = 20 gallons per second.

We know that the basin can hold 260 gallons of water. To find the time it takes to fill the basin, we can divide 260 by the rate at which water from the waterfall enters the basin and then take the reciprocal.

\begin{align*}
\frac{260}{20} = 13.0 \text{ seconds} \\
\frac{1}{13.0} = 0.07692
\end{align*}

The time it takes to fill the basin with water from the waterfall is 13.0 seconds. \boxed{13.0}

